{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1775347173,"nonce":"Io3+GTKpVv89PdFBK1mMQNCr29c=","title":"Detect and repair empty git-bug lamport clock files on watcher startup.","message":"If `.git/git-bug/clocks/bugs-edit` or `bugs-create` is empty (0 bytes), ALL git-bug operations fail with `Error: EOF`. This happens when the process is killed during a write. The watcher and all CLI commands become non-functional until manually repaired.\n\nSee docs/gitbug-clock-corruption.md for full investigation.\n\n- tests/test_git_bug_clock_repair.py::test_detect_empty_clock_file\n  Assert: detect_corrupt_clocks() returns list of corrupt clock filenames when file is empty\n- tests/test_git_bug_clock_repair.py::test_repair_edit_clock_from_refs\n  Assert: after repair, bugs-edit contains the max edit-clock value from bug refs\n- tests/test_git_bug_clock_repair.py::test_repair_create_clock_from_refs\n  Assert: after repair, bugs-create contains the max create-clock value from bug refs\n- tests/test_git_bug_clock_repair.py::test_healthy_clocks_not_touched\n  Assert: detect_corrupt_clocks() returns empty list when files are valid\n\n- adapters/trackers/git_bug.py (modify — add clock repair method)\n- host/watcher/host_watcher.py (modify — call repair on startup)\n\n1. Add `repair_lamport_clocks(repo_dir)` to `adapters/trackers/git_bug.py`:\n   - Check `.git/git-bug/clocks/bugs-edit` and `bugs-create`\n   - If empty: scan all `refs/bugs/` tip commits, extract max clock values from tree entries\n   - Write repaired values to clock files\n   - Log a warning when repair is needed\n2. Call `repair_lamport_clocks()` in `HostWatcher.__init__()` or `run()` before first tracker use\n3. Also call it in `host/cli.py` before tracker operations as a safety net\n\nSee adapters/trackers/git_bug.py for existing git-bug CLI wrappers.\n\nREQ: REQ-025 (git-bug lock/reliability)","files":null}]}